{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Bring.</b> The words of the prophet to Moab: before this trouble comes upon you, bring to your soul counsel:" "<b>Counsel.</b> A noun on the pattern of בכח האכילה (1 Kings 19:8), from the root of פלילים (Deuteronomy 32:31):" "<b>Your shadow.</b> That you hide Israel when they flee to you as outcasts, from their place:" "<b>Wandering.</b> To you — do not reveal:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "Hebrew text cited as 'מלכים א' י\"ט ח'׳; normalized."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:59.449247659Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}